    <UnitTestResult executionId="9b250b2a-5400-4ff5-864a-1333ad64e8f5" testId="ac78c2b4-c6e6-85eb-f711-8ba9604cb46f" testName="ShineMusic.Tests.Acceptance.PlaylistBatchScaleTests.Preview_import_and_enqueue_match_the_retained_legacy_reference_with_chunk_bounded_sql(size: 1000)" computerName="暖树" duration="00:00:24.4735515" startTime="2026-11-26T08:53:51.8422228+08:00" endTime="2026-11-26T08:54:16.3157786+08:00" testType="13cdc9d9-ddb5-4fa4-a97d-d965ccfc6d4b" outcome="Passed" testListId="8c84fa94-04c1-424b-9868-57a2d4851a1d" relativeResultsDirectory="9b250b2a-5400-4ff5-864a-1333ad64e8f5">
      <Output>
        <StdOut>SQLite synthetic size=1000, published matches=500, unmatched=500; one observation per workflow after matching warmup.&#xD;
Legacy reference is the pre-batch per-input matcher and import/enqueue loops retained below in test code, not a second execution of removed production code.&#xD;
Both variants read the same synthetic catalog; the extra playlists/queue rows they create do not participate in catalog matching. No source provider search is enabled.&#xD;
preview: legacy SQL=2000 (SELECT=2000, INSERT=0, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=1581.965, transactionMs=N/A; batch SQL=6 (SELECT=6, INSERT=0, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=15.283, transactionMs=N/A&#xD;
import: legacy SQL=3501 (SELECT=2500, INSERT=1001, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=809.690, transactionMs=807.649; batch SQL=27 (SELECT=6, INSERT=21, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=106.179, transactionMs=104.981&#xD;
enqueue: legacy SQL=2001 (SELECT=2000, INSERT=1, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=1633.663, transactionMs=N/A; batch SQL=16 (SELECT=6, INSERT=10, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=81.214, transactionMs=65.647&#xD;
settlement: legacy SQL=4001 (SELECT=2501, INSERT=500, UPDATE=500, DELETE=500), totalMs=8385.921, transactionMs=N/A; batch SQL=525 (SELECT=9, INSERT=10, UPDATE=6, DELETE=500), totalMs=10063.764, transactionMs=N/A&#xD;
Settlement baseline is restricted to this seeded scenario: half of completed tasks reference a published import, half reference pending_review; its retained test loop reads each task/import and writes each link/delete/status individually. It is not a reproduction of every old settlement branch. The batch implementation intentionally retains one fenced DELETE per promoted row.&#xD;
Transaction milliseconds are available only when measured around BeginTranAsync through successful CommitTranAsync (legacy test stopwatch / production structured diagnostic). N/A means no separate accurate observation; legacy enqueue used one bulk command without an explicit service transaction.&#xD;
Total times include AOP instrumentation and local SQLite I/O. These single samples do not establish PostgreSQL latency, network effects, P95, concurrency behavior or an acceleration multiple. No timing threshold is asserted.</StdOut>
      </Output>
